{"format":1,"seq":40,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm thinking about how to surface a small scalar field like \"outcome\" in the result summary line, so something like showing \"outcome: pending\" alongside the field count rather than burying it in the list.\n\nI also need to check whether npm.run has access to the script name through the renderer's context, and I should fix the pluralization for \"1 check is still pending\" and figure out how attempts should be derived.\n\nFor attempts, I'm thinking when no explicit count is given, the deadline alone should govern how many polls happen rather than capping at a fixed number — deriving a default from timeoutMs and intervalMs but leaving it unbounded since the deadline already constrains it. I need to check the existing test expecting requestedAttempts: 120 to make sure this doesn't break it.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01CH7Z3GbFYnuMH6aCxvYAJw","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Inspect renderer context types, npm global, and wait tests\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { read, search } }) => {\n  const [types, npmG, t1, t2, t3, ctxUse] = await Promise.all([\n    read(\"src/renderers/types.ts\", { format: \"raw\" }),\n    search(\"script\", { path: \"src/globals\", glob: \"**/npm*\", limit: 30 }),\n    read(\"test/functions/workflow-pr-checks.test.ts\", { format: \"raw\" }),\n    read(\"test/functions/workflow-wait.test.ts\", { format: \"raw\" }),\n    read(\"test/globals/npm.test.ts\", { format: \"raw\", offset: 1, limit: 60 }),\n    search(\"args\", { path: \"src/renderers\", glob: \"*-result.ts\", limit: 30 }),\n  ]);\n  return { types: types.content, npmG: npmG.matches.map(m => `${m.file}:${m.line} ${m.text}`), t1: t1.content, t2: t2.content, t3: t3.content, ctxUse: ctxUse.matches.map(m => `${m.file}:${m.line} ${m.text}`) };\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","mod